{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/373110-does-a-botch-on-a-lvl-5-castigate-power-which-separates-shadow-and-psyche-actually","id":373110,"title":"does a botch on a lvl 5 castigate power which separates shadow and psyche actually","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-16T17:33:14-08:00","id":373110,"title":"does a botch on a lvl 5 castigate power which separates shadow and psyche actually","content":"causes transcendence?<br /> <br /> this is how i think of it.<br /> <br /> first according to this pwoers rules in order to remain on the underworld the wraith must roll the passions. the same thing that must be resolved in order to transcend the normal way.<br /> <br /> second when a ferryman(created by a similar ritual) or pasiphae dies the ferryman immediately transcends and the pasiphae descends to oblivion. <br /> <br /> third the book says that a &quot;wraith destroyed this way(botching this power) does not show any of the outwards signs of transcendence<b> which usually</b> appear. the word usually here seems to imply that it does not always happen.<br /> <br /> 4th IIRC it is stated in a few sources that a wraith with no shadow transcends very soon. this is normally meant to mean having a rating of 0 but the example of the ferryman seems to imply that you can transcend so long as you have no shadow inside you. after all technically speaking in both cases the rating is 0.<br /> <br /> 5 at this point it'just me wildly speculating but i think that the only difference is that during a transcendence the shadow(perhaps) dissolves completely only minimally(if at all) feeding oblivion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T19:49:32-08:00","id":373980,"title":"","content":"I don't have the core <b>Wraith</b> book handy, but I doubt it. By comparison to other creatures with similar powers, I think a botch is more likely to cause a brutal, uncontrollable Catharsis. One where the psyche can't even spend willpower to reign in the shadow.<br /> <br /> Transcendence is a <i>big</i> deal. The apotheosis, the pinnacle, of everything the wraith had hoped to achieve in life. And the resolution of his (or her) regrets and unfinished business. If screwing up Castigate could short-circuit the process, wraiths would've found a way to deliberately duplicate the effect centuries ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T01:19:06-08:00","id":374115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/373110-does-a-botch-on-a-lvl-5-castigate-power-which-separates-shadow-and-psyche-actually?p=373980#post373980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the core <b>Wraith</b> book handy, but I doubt it. By comparison to other creatures with similar powers, I think a botch is more likely to cause a brutal, uncontrollable Catharsis. One where the psyche can't even spend willpower to reign in the shadow.<br /> <br /> Transcendence is a <i>big</i> deal. The apotheosis, the pinnacle, of everything the wraith had hoped to achieve in life. And the resolution of his (or her) regrets and unfinished business. If screwing up Castigate could short-circuit the process, wraiths would've found a way to deliberately duplicate the effect centuries ago.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> what im saying is NOT in the core book. it's a special lvl 5 castigate power that if you botch it has this result a psyche andshadow separated and the psyche needds to make a passion roll every hour or ..disappear. im arguing that based on evidence this may be transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T08:04:16-08:00","id":374278,"title":"","content":"Well in Kindred of the East, the creation process of the Kuei-Jin has the soul of the recently deceased splitting in two, with the P'o (the Shadow) being dragged into one of the 1000 Hells while the Hun (the Psyche) is left behind in the Underworld. While the Hun may be free of the P'o they begin to slowly wither a way and if the P'o doesn't escape and rejoin with the Hun and their corpse the Hun will fade away to nothing and P'o will be trapped forever. That is not Transcendence or Oblivion, that's merely non-existence.<br /> <br /> Similarly the Ferrymen that have a ritual that separates Shadow from the Psyche and is an important part in becoming a Ferrymen. But they don't purse their own Transcedence and might not even be possible for them in their state. Overcoming your Shadow, which wants the opposite of Transcendence, is a part of that. Plus the Shadow is ultimately a part of the wraith. It may be born of all the negative aspects of a person but they are still a part of the person. Removing a Shadow might just prevent Transcendence simply because the wraith is missing a piece of one's soul, preventing them from crossing over as they are incomplete.<br /> <br /> In fact the particular art you mentioned it specifically states that there is none of the usual lightshow that occurs during Transcendence, meaning it isn't Transcendence. After all there is no shortcut to overcoming your personal demons and baggage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:42:39-08:00","id":382016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/373110-does-a-botch-on-a-lvl-5-castigate-power-which-separates-shadow-and-psyche-actually?p=374278#post374278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in Kindred of the East, the creation process of the Kuei-Jin has the soul of the recently deceased splitting in two, with the P'o (the Shadow) being dragged into one of the 1000 Hells while the Hun (the Psyche) is left behind in the Underworld. While the Hun may be free of the P'o they begin to slowly wither a way and if the P'o doesn't escape and rejoin with the Hun and their corpse the Hun will fade away to nothing and P'o will be trapped forever. That is not Transcendence or Oblivion, that's merely non-existence.<br /> <br /> Similarly the Ferrymen that have a ritual that separates Shadow from the Psyche and is an important part in becoming a Ferrymen. But they don't purse their own Transcedence and might not even be possible for them in their state. Overcoming your Shadow, which wants the opposite of Transcendence, is a part of that. Plus the Shadow is ultimately a part of the wraith. It may be born of all the negative aspects of a person but they are still a part of the person. Removing a Shadow might just prevent Transcendence simply because the wraith is missing a piece of one's soul, preventing them from crossing over as they are incomplete.<br /> <br /> In fact the particular art you mentioned it specifically states that there is none of the usual lightshow that occurs during Transcendence, meaning it isn't Transcendence. After all there is no shortcut to overcoming your personal demons and baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> whena ferryman dies he transcends immediately andthe pasiphae(shadow) is obliviated. that's why im wandering whether al lthat it takes is to forcibly separate those 2.<br /> <br /> after all by definition a wraith whose shadow drops to 0 transcends very soon&quot;thus making it a short chronicle..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:57:07-07:00","id":446009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/373110-does-a-botch-on-a-lvl-5-castigate-power-which-separates-shadow-and-psyche-actually?p=382016#post382016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> whena ferryman dies he transcends immediately andthe pasiphae(shadow) is obliviated. that's why im wandering whether al lthat it takes is to forcibly separate those 2.<br /> <br /> after all by definition a wraith whose shadow drops to 0 transcends very soon&quot;thus making it a short chronicle..</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no. Ferrymen transcend because they don't have fetters, and have probably resolved all their other ties to the living world. They've done decades or centuries of good works.<br /> <br /> A wraith who has her Shadow separated would not be in the same situation. She might head straight to Oblivion as her soul is torn apart, or might end up with a Pasiphae, but as this is the result of a botch, the outcome wouldn't be neat. I'd suggest hefty penalties for the latter option. More likely, she'll just enter a destruction harrowing or become a spectre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:57:26-07:00","id":446182,"title":"","content":"is having resolved your fetters an actual metaphysical requirement of becoming a ferryman? or do they just do it to ensure that recruits are already on the way to transcendence?<br /> <br /> anyway it's been some time so ill need to recheck the book with that castigate power but i think it implies that the wraith/shadow literally disappears","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:04:24-07:00","id":446195,"title":"","content":"It's not a requirement, nor is it mentioned anywhere, but the Ferrymen don't recruit often and prefer specific 'types' of person. I'm just positing that Ferrymen might automatically transcend because of the kind of people they tend to be, rather than simply because no Shadow = transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}